It&#x27;d matter if this certification came with an extensive test suite guaranteeing some degree of compliance. Instead, you have macOS defaulting to an antediluvian bash as &#x2F;bin&#x2F;sh full of ridiculous bugs like this:<p><pre><code>  $ cat test.sh
  var=
  echo &quot;${var+{\}}&quot;
  cat &lt;&lt;EOF
  ${var+\&quot;foo\&quot;}
  EOF
  $ &#x2F;bin&#x2F;sh test.sh
  {\}
  \&quot;foo\&quot;
  $ &#x2F;bin&#x2F;dash test.sh
  {}
  &quot;foo&quot;
</code></pre>
Note that they even ship dash as a much better &#x2F;bin&#x2F;sh...
